WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.740
Three identical trays each hold one pouch and

00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:04.670
two loose counters.

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:07.770
Every pouch holds the same number of counters.

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:11.090
Altogether the trays contain twenty-one counters.

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:13.430
How many counters are in each pouch?

00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:20.390
The three trays are identical, so they share the

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:21.780
twenty-one counters equally.

00:00:22.730 --> 00:00:24.620
Twenty-one divided by three is seven.

00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:26.780
Each tray holds seven counters.

00:00:27.940 --> 00:00:30.530
In one tray, two of the seven counters are loose.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:31.890
The rest are in the pouch.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:33.890
Seven minus two is five.

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:36.090
Each pouch holds five counters.

00:00:37.230 --> 00:00:39.530
In symbols: three lots of a pouch plus

00:00:39.530 --> 00:00:40.880
two equals twenty-one.

00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:43.480
So a pouch plus two equals seven,

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:45.140
and a pouch equals five.

00:00:45.690 --> 00:00:48.100
The bars and the equation tell the same story.

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:50.020
There is a second route.

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:52.580
Take away all six loose counters first.

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:55.650
Fifteen counters remain, shared by three

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:57.020
pouches: five each.

00:00:57.730 --> 00:00:59.780
Two different orders, the same answer,

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:01.040
which is a good check.

00:01:02.030 --> 00:01:04.780
You can share first, or remove the extras first.

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:09.050
Rebuild both routes, then try this: four identical bags

00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:11.760
each hold one box and three loose marbles,

00:01:11.930 --> 00:01:13.520
making forty marbles altogether.

00:01:14.190 --> 00:01:15.840
How many marbles are in each box?
